    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d505-a2">

                <pb facs="0566" n="516" sameAs="frus:frus1894/pg516"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Document No. 2.—To the legation of Portugal at Rio
                        de Janeiro.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1894-03-12"><hi rendition="#small-caps">March</hi> 12,
                        1894</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Portuguese Government does not wish its agents there to do any act which can be
                    disagreeable to the constituted Government; therefore we must know how the
                    Brazilian Government will accept the intervention of Commandant Castilho to
                    treat of capitulation. You will please, therefore, ascertain, informing me
                    immediately, so that proper instructions may be given you. In order that asylum
                    for Gama and officers may be effectuated, it is indispensable for Castilho to
                    reach an understanding with commanders of foreign vessels.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hintze Ribeiro.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
